Let a batch use its full width on files with many subtitles

A run reported "2/4 workers" on ten-track episodes. Two causes:

1. The candidate scan stopped after limit*4 jobs. With ten subtitles per episode those candidates
   covered two media files, so the wave could never be wider than two, whatever the setting. The
   scan now scales with the worker count (bounded by an absolute ceiling so a large queue cannot
   stall a scheduler pass).
2. An extra "this job is heavy" veto in the claim check overrode the sharing policy that decides
   whether two subtitles of one file may overlap, so a file's later subtitles always queued behind
   the first - even after their reference subtitle had been extracted. The policy is now the only
   decision-maker, and it says yes when the audio analysis is stored or the reference is cached.

The extracted reference subtitle is also written atomically now (temporary file, then moved), so
two subtitles of one file extracting it simultaneously cannot leave a half-written file behind.

Checks: 132, ALL PASS. Two existing checks had encoded the veto and were updated to the intended
contract, with a new check that a refusing policy still prevents sharing.

Version 1.1.0.35.
